From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:20:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmp-report: declare the ANE DVFS hooks as absent

The ANE driver in aurora-silicon/linux integration/aurora (ane_perf.c,
from 996ef2aef5 "accel/ane: replace CPU QoS boost with scoped performance
requests") calls apple_pmp_report_ane_available() and
apple_pmp_report_ane_perf(). Their implementation in pmp-report.c needs
the T6041 "ane-dvfs" report layout and the deferred-request machinery of
a newer PMP report driver than this base has; three of its four hunks
conflict with this base's pmp-report.c.

Declare both as inline functions that report the channel as absent
(-EOPNOTSUPP, no clock held), on every SoC and configuration, so the ANE
driver builds and runs at the firmware's own clock without a PMP vote.
No PMP behaviour changes. ANE DVFS on the T8132 is a separate parity
item (J604 ADT /arm-io/ane has pmp-virt-notify = 1 and the
ANE-SYS-V-PMP gate): TO-VERIFY against the J604 PMP report layout.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h
index 25049fcd73..1104d85c09 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h
@@ -13,6 +13,24 @@
 struct device_node;
 struct device;
 
+/*
+ * ANE DVFS requests through the PMP report region (Aurora 996ef2aef5) need
+ * the T6041 "ane-dvfs" report layout, which this kernel's PMP report driver
+ * does not carry. Report the channel as absent on every SoC: the ANE driver
+ * then runs at the firmware's own clock and holds no request.
+ */
+static inline int apple_pmp_report_ane_available(const struct device_node *np)
+{
+	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+}
+
+static inline int apple_pmp_report_ane_perf(const struct device_node *np,
+					    struct device *owner, unsigned int level, bool *held)
+{
+	*held = false;
+	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+}
+
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_APPLE_PMP_REPORT)
 int apple_pmp_report_wait_supplier_ready(struct device *supplier, unsigned int timeout_ms);
 /* Caller holds the PMP owner's vote lock and keeps the supplier bound. */
